# MLIR MCP Server Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values as needed

# === Option 1: Auto-Detection (No Config Needed) ===
# If your MLIR is in a standard location, no configuration needed!
# Auto-detected locations:
#   - /opt/ttmlir-toolchain/bin
#   - /usr/local/llvm/bin
#   - /usr/local/bin
#   - /opt/llvm/bin
#   - ~/llvm-project/build/bin

# === Option 2: Simple Single Installation ===
# Specify just the bin directory
# MLIR_TOOLCHAIN_PATH=/path/to/llvm/build/bin

# === Option 3: Multiple MLIR Installations (RECOMMENDED) ===
# Automatically configures everything: tools, Python bindings, libraries
# Colon-separated list of MLIR installation ROOT directories
#
# Each installation should have this structure:
#   <root>/bin/                      - Tools (mlir-opt, proj-opt, etc.)
#   <root>/lib/                      - Shared libraries
#   <root>/python_packages/mlir_core/ - Python bindings
#
# Example with main LLVM + custom "TT" project:
MLIR_INSTALLATIONS=/path/to/llvm-build:/path/to/tt-build
#
# This automatically:
# 1. Searches all bin/ directories for tools
# 2. Adds all Python bindings to PYTHONPATH
# 3. Adds all lib/ directories to LD_LIBRARY_PATH/DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH
# 4. Makes all tools available (mlir-opt, tt-opt, etc.)
#
# NO manual PYTHONPATH or library path setup needed!
